# =============================================================================
# dnsmasq Syslog-style Log — Format Documentation
# =============================================================================
# Auto-detected when BOTH keywords appear in the first 600 bytes:
#   "dnsmasq"   "query["
#
# No CSV header row — each line is parsed by regex.
# Lines beginning with '#' are treated as comments and ignored.
#
# Required line pattern (regex):
#   <syslog-ts> <host> dnsmasq[<pid>]: query[<TYPE>] <domain> from <ip>
#
# Standard field  ←  Extracted from
# --------------  -----------------------------------------------------------
# timestamp       ← syslog timestamp  (e.g. "Jan 15 08:00:00")
# domain          ← FQDN after "query[TYPE] "  (trailing dot stripped)
# query_type      ← record type inside query[...]  (A, AAAA, TXT, MX, …)
# query_length    ← computed from len(domain)
# subdomain_count ← computed from label count
# response_size   ← defaults to 0 (not present in query-only logs)
#
# Example line:
#   Jan 15 08:00:00 router dnsmasq[1234]: query[A] google.com from 10.0.0.1
# =============================================================================
Jan 15 08:00:00 router dnsmasq[1234]: query[A] google.com from 192.168.1.0
Jan 15 08:00:10 router dnsmasq[1234]: query[TXT] a8f3kq2.tunnel.example.com from 192.168.1.1
Jan 15 08:00:20 router dnsmasq[1234]: query[AAAA] github.com from 192.168.1.2
Jan 15 08:00:30 router dnsmasq[1234]: query[NULL] exfildata.evil.io from 192.168.1.3
